   "speaker": "Mitch Fifield",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-12-11",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The mover proposed that the Senate sit continuously from 8 pm on 12 December 2013 until all 13 listed bills—including those to repeal the carbon tax and the Minerals Resource Rent Tax—are finally considered, with only government business allowed. The Australian Labor Party and the Australian Greens were accused of delaying the vote to deny the coalition’s election mandate to abolish the carbon tax."
